# This repository is developed on Windows, where git is commonly configured with
# core.autocrlf=true and rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. That is
# right for the Go sources, which nothing but Windows ever compiles, and wrong
# for anything that is deployed somewhere else.
#
# The Blueprint extension is the thing that is deployed somewhere else. It is
# copied onto a Pterodactyl Panel, which is Linux, and its installer is run there
# by bash -- which does not tolerate a carriage return at the end of a line and
# does not say so clearly when it finds one. `set -e` becomes "invalid option",
# every other line becomes "$'\r': command not found", and the first `if` block
# fails at its `elif` with a syntax error, none of which names the cause.
#
# So the whole extension is pinned to LF regardless of how anyone's git is
# configured, and so is any shell script anywhere in the tree.

blueprint/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Marked before the rule above can try to normalise them.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
